y: Christian Pasin &lt;christian.pasin@displaylink.com&gt; Tested-by: Christian Pasin &lt;christian.pasin@displaylink.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328991" owner_email="christian.pasin@displaylink.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/91/328991/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I697ebfccf302a4a1cd60ba9a2a03f50497145a70" commit="0e70a507f104d5ab68309720330ab31ea4e30d3c" commit_message="goofy: show test list exceptions on startup  Currently when a test list file contains a syntax error, a cryptic message occurs telling the user that their chosen test list ID is not valid, i.e.:    An error occurred while starting the factory test system.   Factory testing cannot proceed.    'main' is not a valid test list ID (available IDs are [ ... ])  It's quite common to make syntax (or other) errors while editing a test list file, so it would be useful to be able to see what these errors are without having to open up factory.log.  This patch adds a short traceback (only the last frame) for each test invalid list file in the Goofy startup &quot;alert box&quot;, e.g.:    An error occurred while starting the factory test system.   Factory testing cannot proceed.    Error in test list file (.../test_lists/generic_rrt.py):   Traceback (most recent call last):     [short traceback here]    Error in test list file (.../test_lists/main.py):   Traceback (most recent call last):     [short traceback here]    'main' is not a valid test list ID (available IDs are [ ... ])  The regular factory.log file retains full tracebacks for each test list exception as before.  BUG=None TEST=Manually on DUT  Change-Id: I697ebfccf302a4a1cd60ba9a2a03f50497145a70 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328900 Commit-Ready: Jo